course: dictionary
lesson: 2669
title: Diabolical: wicked or just dreadful?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Diabolical» is a strong word. Its first meaning is very wicked or cruel, as if the Devil had planned it. In «a diabolical plan», the plan is cunning and evil.
explain: Look at the words around it. Villains in stories have «diabolical plots» and «diabolical laughs», so the clues tell you the word is about evil and cleverness.
explain: Adults in Britain also use «diabolical» in a lighter, informal way. «The traffic was diabolical» does not mean the traffic was evil. It means the traffic was extremely bad. Ask yourself: is anyone being wicked here? If not, the word probably means very bad.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. «The traffic was wicked» sounds silly, but «The traffic was extremely bad» fits. The word comes from «diabolos», Greek for devil.
fact: «Diabolical» means very wicked or cruel, as if done by the Devil.
fact: In informal British English, «diabolical» can also mean extremely bad or of very poor quality.
fact: «Diabolical» comes from «diabolos», the Greek word for devil.
fact: The adverb is «diabolically», as in «diabolically clever».
fact: The diabolical ironclad beetle of the USA has armour so strong that scientists found it could take a force about 39,000 times its own weight.
exercise: Villains in stories make «diabolical plots». What does diabolical mean here? | Very slow and tired | Very kind and gentle | Very bright and shiny | *Very wicked and cruel
exercise: Dad says after a match, «That refereeing was diabolical.» What does he mean? | *Extremely bad, with terrible decisions | Calm and quiet | A devil was seen on the pitch | Lovely and fair
exercise: Read: «The diabolical ironclad beetle of the USA has armour that scientists found could take a force about 39,000 times its weight.» What does the sentence tell you about the beetle? | It can fly very fast | It is kind to other insects | *Its armour is very strong and it cannot fly | It is small and soft
test: Which sentence uses diabolical to mean very wicked? | *«The villain's diabolical plan frightened the whole kingdom.» | «The bus was diabolical and always late.» | «The soup was diabolical, far too salty.» | «The sky was a diabolical shade of blue.»
test: The word diabolical comes from which language? | *Greek | French | Dutch | Scots
exam: Which word could replace diabolical in «The traffic was diabolical» without changing the meaning? | Happy | *Terrible | Quiet | Tall
